WEBVTT

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.530
Hey!

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.130
I know it's you!

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.800
No fireworks
allowed in the library.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.330
If I catch you again,
you'll be punished!

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.300
Jeez.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:57.030
I want to see you but I can't
see you because it hurts so much.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:01.200
I'm sure I must
be missing something...

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.430
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:08.530
(Yami, the Hat and the Book traveler)
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:15.460
I had always believed
that what I saw before me...

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:22.260
...was the only truth there was.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:30.100
But now I know
there isn't just one world.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:39.560
There are a thousand worlds called
"if" and I don't know which way to turn.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.460
I want to see you but
I can't see you; where are you now?

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:48.600
I'll find you no matter the cost.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:56.360
I've wandered into the
labyrinth of your eyes.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:00.360
Even if the darkness bars my path...

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:06.360
...even if my weak heart
is led astray, I won't give up.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:11.330
I'll keep searching for you.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:26.900
Hey, how long has
she been here anyway?

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.730
Jill
Hey, how long has
she been here anyway?

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.200
Jill

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:36.200
The reason I'm in
charge of this library...

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.830
Ouch!

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.930
She was already here, I think.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:47.830
I think!

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:55.230
The reason why I
was put in charge...

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.160
It's her fault!

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:00.630
Eve!

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.460
I'll never forgive her!

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.230
Yamiyanma!

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.130
Papa?

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:31.060
Wow, you look like Yamiyanma!

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.100
Yamiyanma?

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:42.260
Yep, Yamiyanma.
The person who l-o-v-e-d, me!

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:44.830
It was a long time ago, though.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:47.900
What are you talking about?

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.000
Well, how come a human is here?

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:55.030
Ordinary humans
can't just come here.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.060
I was just looking for Hatsumi.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.300
Hatsumi?

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:06.830
Oh, that must be like the 88
nights of summers' approach...

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:10.130
That's the tea picking song,
"Chatsumi", not Hatsumi!

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:16.030
I knew you were behind this,
you fluffy yellow dumpling!

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:20.700
It's complicated,
don't just blame me.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.860
Well, I'll take it
easy on you this time.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.730
Lilith, do you have
a fever or something?

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.000
Stop it!

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.230
I don't know why...

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.100
I didn't think I was into girls?

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.260
Oh, my heart is
beating so fast...

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.600
What is your name?

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:07.260
Her name is Hazuki and a person
named Hatsumi is missing so I was...

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.060
Hazuki, let's go!

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.860
Hey, where are we going?

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:22.300
Um, let's see... oh, I found it!

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.830
This book is a hideout of Lilith.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.960
I've kept this book
here for a long time.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.200
What's that?

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.300
Tasty!

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:54.000
How do you like this place,
Lilith's favorite place?

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.200
Why am I wearing this?

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.460
Did you prefer a bikini?

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.600
That's not it.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.860
No wonder, you've
got a great body.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.130
You should show more skin.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.300
I am going home.

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:16.800
Hey, Hazuki!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.660
Wait up! I've gotta talk to you!

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:29.030
What do you think of Lilith?

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.260
Weirdo.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:34.230
Oh, don't be so mean.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.000
Okay, Ha-zu-ki!

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:38.700
I am going home.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.500
Hey, Hazuki!

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:47.500
Listen up, I think
I've fallen in love.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:48.730
With who?

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:49.660
With you.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:50.830
Stop joking, okay?

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:52.830
I am not joking.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.600
I am serious, you're
the only one for me!

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.230
If you abandon me, I'll....

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.630
I'll die.

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:06.130
If you want to die,
I won't stop you.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.030
Thank you.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:48.730
Let me go!

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:51.030
No, I won't.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.560
Give me a break already!

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:01.130
Get off of me!

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.430
No, because you
remind me of Yamiyama.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.060
Who is this Yamiyama?

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:11.600
The person who created this
world, also made Lilith's hat.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.460
And the person
who abandoned her.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.630
Now, let's go to another world.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:35.560
Secret hide-out part two!

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:37.530
Take me back where I was.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:42.030
Isn't it exciting to be wearing
swimsuits in a place like this?

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:48.100
Oh my heart, right here, like this...

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:51.200
Stop it.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:52.900
No, I won't.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.100
Who is Hatsumi?

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:01.100
Hatsumi, my sister... disappeared.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:02.460
Really?

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.630
On her 16th birthday.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:08.230
By any chance
does Hatsumi have...

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:10.360
...have a big
forehead like this?

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:14.300
That's Eve.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:15.200
Eve?

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:20.830
Also known as foreheaddy.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.500
The person I hate the most.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:26.700
She foisted this
hat and library on me...

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.600
...and took off to
travel in the book worlds.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.160
This Hatsumi person must be the
secret identity of Eve, no doubt.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.630
Where is she now?

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.600
She's probably having fun
somewhere in another world.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:39.200
She's still alive?

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:42.000
That forehead girl
can't die even if you tried.

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:47.360
I will find her, no matter what.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:50.730
This is the first time in so long
that I feel like looking for Eve.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.300
I can help you.

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:53.900
I can handle it by myself.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:59.330
Without me, you
can't go to other worlds.

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:07.860
Look over there!

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:14.830
Run!

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:32.530
Oh, sister Lilith, are
you off to another world?

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:35.030
Then, I'm more than
happy to accompany you.

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:38.560
If so, bring me a
book with strong souma.

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:40.000
Are you leaving soon?

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:40.900
Soon.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.930
After I'm done punishing her.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:50.060
Well, well...

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:53.000
Looks like a pretty rough place.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:54.900
What is this place?

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:59.130
It's the beginning of
our romantic journey!

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.600
Oh, wait up!

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:07.230
That is how
Hazuki's journey began.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:13.160
At this time, let us journey
back to a much older story.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:31.830
It's done!

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:38.330
Birdies look! Isn't it pretty?

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.630
Why?

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:56.930
Is it dead?

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:00.830
Gar!

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:03.100
It's boring when they die.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:07.700
How could you? It was
singing so beautifully.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:14.600
What is so lovely about a
bird that sings for everybody?

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.960
I want a bird that
only sings for me.

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:25.000
Jill!

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:46.160
How did you do that?
Is that magic?

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:54.500
Since you came, it's been
such nice weather, thank god!

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:58.700
The kids here make
so much dirty laundry.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.530
So, you really can't speak?

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:07.000
Poor thing.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:11.230
Well, it's better than
some people with big mouths.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.460
Are you talking about yourself?

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:14.600
I'm talking about you!

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.730
There's a really
nice river near here.

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:20.900
There's lots of fish, too.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.260
Let's go, Jill!

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:25.160
Hurry up, Jill!

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:31.600
Go on, but be
back by supper time.

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:33.860
Thank you!

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:35.200
Let's go!

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:43.960
We made plenty
enough for second helpings!

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.400
It's cold.

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:21.800
Hey Jill, over here!

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:39.200
Are you trying to stop me?

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:41.630
Why?

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:54.700
Okay, I won't do it again.

00:15:56.860 --> 00:16:01.030
In return, teach me your magic.

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:07.900
That magic you used to revive the
bird and stop the bleeding on my knee.

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:10.500
Isn't that magic?

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:16.030
If you teach me, I promise I
won't kill the birds anymore.

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:21.800
Why not!?

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:35.460
You are the thunder,
a blade that sweeps...

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:38.930
...with a dark shadow
followed by the lightning.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:43.660
You can destroy the
spark of life in a flash...

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:47.130
...but you'll
never be able to restore it.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:56.700
Enough! I hate you!

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:02.130
What happened, Jill?

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:14.760
Hey Gar, don't you like Jill?

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:22.200
I like her a lot,
she smells really nice.

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:26.900
And when I'm with her,
it warms my heart.

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:30.900
It must feel that
way to have a mother.

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:34.000
I wouldn't want somebody
like that to be my mom.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:34.830
But...

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:36.160
Don't talk to me anymore!

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.560
Wow, your magic is so great!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:25.030
It's... your power?

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:30.500
The power of a soft breeze
makes everybody feel better?

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:33.730
Jill, really?

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:38.360
So nice!

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:49.360
Gar?

00:18:57.330 --> 00:19:01.360
Why, why not me?

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:03.730
Say something.

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:05.500
Answer me, Jill!

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:19.100
I want you to love me, just me!

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:33.730
I can't find Gar.

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:34.630
I think.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.030
No!

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:42.100
Ritsuko! What happened?

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.260
Talk to me!

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:47.500
The shock must
have been too great.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.760
She lost her memory.

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:56.430
10 years later

00:20:57.660 --> 00:20:59.960
Everybody, lunch is ready!

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:11.360
Don't cry, okay?

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:15.660
Come on, Ritsuko!

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:20.960
Seeing you do that,
reminds me of Jill.

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:25.400
She left so suddenly.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:28.830
You sure you don't
know where she went?

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:35.030
Jill, Gargantua...

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:39.060
Where have you gone without me?

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:53.300
I will offer up an eternal prayer.

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:59.730
I will never give up on what matters.

00:22:02.560 --> 00:22:07.200
I will go there, praying.

00:22:07.760 --> 00:22:14.030
No matter the distance
between us, I will catch you.

00:22:14.300 --> 00:22:21.860
That's a promise between you and I.

00:22:22.060 --> 00:22:29.200
Crying, cradling my memories,...

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:35.700
...won't help even one
of my feelings to reach you.

00:22:37.300 --> 00:22:44.730
I will offer up an eternal prayer.

00:22:44.930 --> 00:22:51.360
I will never give up on what matters.

00:22:53.330 --> 00:23:00.260
I will find the dawn
between you and I,...

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:08.700
...and meet the approaching daybreak.

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:13.800
I will go there, praying.

00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:17.730
Gargantua's past
was so traumatic...

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:18.730
How sad.

00:23:19.130 --> 00:23:21.160
Let's take a look
at the next book.

00:23:50.100 --> 00:23:53.260
Next Time: Mariel
Yami, the Hat and the Book Traveler.

00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:55.960
We hope you enjoy
the next story as well.
